<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle sell $103-$103.50/drsd-private.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle sell $103-$103.50/drsd-private.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot cattle sold mostly at $103.00 per cwt on a dressed basis, with a few loads at $103.50 in light to moderate volume near midday on Wednesday, market sources said.</p>
<p>Sales were steady to down $0.50 from Tuesday. There also were possible sales at $64.00 on a live basis, which would be unchanged from Tuesday, sources said.</p>
<p>An estimated 8,000 steers and heifers had sold, which brought the week-to-date movement close to 43,000 head, the sources said.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
